.TH OTPME-ROLE 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-role \- manage OTPme roles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-role
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIrole\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-role
manages roles in the OTPme system. Roles are groups of tokens or other roles that can be nested.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Role Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fB\-\-groups\fR \fIgroup1,group2\fR] [\fB\-\-roles\fR \fIrole1,role2\fR] \fIrole\fR
Create a new role. Optionally add it directly to groups or other roles.
.TP
.B del \fIrole\fR
Delete a role.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIrole\fR]
Display role information. Without arguments, shows all roles.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List roles, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIrole\fR
Enable a disabled role.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B disable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIrole\fR
Disable a role without deleting it.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B rename \fIrole\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a role.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIrole\fR \fIunit\fR
Move role to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIrole\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Token Assignment
.TP
.B add_token \fR[\fB\-i\fR \fIinterfaces\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-sign\fR] [\fB\-\-sign\fR \fB\-\-tags\fR \fItag1,tag2\fR] [\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-portal\-token\fR] \fIrole\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Add a token to the role. Use \fB\-i\fR to limit login to specific interfaces (e.g. tty, gui, ssh). If the token is the SSO token of a site's portal (its name is that site's \fBdefault_sso_token_name\fR), the tokens the portal manages for the user are added as well, after a confirmation, with the same options. \fB\-\-skip\-portal\-token\fR adds only the given token.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B remove_token \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-sign\fR] [\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-portal\-token\fR] \fIrole\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a token from the role. If the token is the SSO token of a site's portal, the tokens the portal manages for the user are removed as well, after a confirmation, with the same options. \fB\-\-skip\-portal\-token\fR removes only the given token.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B list_tokens \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIrole\fR
List tokens assigned to the role. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Role Nesting
.TP
.B add_role \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIrole\fR \fIchild_role\fR
Add a child role to this role.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B remove_role \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIrole\fR \fIchild_role\fR
Remove a child role from this role.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B list_roles \fR[\fB\-r\fR] \fIrole\fR
List roles assigned to the role. Use \fB\-r\fR for recursive listing.
.TP
.B find_acls \fIrole\fR
Find the ACLs this role holds on other objects.
.TP
.B find_scopes \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIrole\fR
Find OIDC scopes the role is assigned to. \fB\-\-return\-type\fR selects the attribute to return (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B find_shares \fR[\fB\-r\fR] [\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIrole\fR
Find shares granted via this role. \fB\-r\fR walks child roles too.
.SS VLAN Assignment
A role is not assigned a VLAN from here. The VLAN names the role, not the
other way round, so the assignment belongs to the site that runs the network
(see
.BR otpme-vlan (1)):
.PP
.RS
.B otpme-vlan add_role \fIvlan\fR \fIrole\fR
.RE
.PP
Every token, host and device of the role then gets that VLAN during 802.1x
or MAB port authentication, and so does every role nested in it. The more
specific assignment wins: a VLAN naming a token itself beats one naming its
role, and a VLAN naming a nested role beats one naming the role it is nested
in. So a role can be given a VLAN of its own without taking the outer role
out of its VLAN.
.PP
Only VLANs of the site answering the RADIUS request are looked at. Where no
VLAN names the role or its members, the
.B vlans
config parameter of the token, user, host or device decides (see
.BR otpme (7)).
.SS User and Group Listing
.TP
.B list_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIrole\fR
List users of the role. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B list_dynamic_groups \fIrole\fR
List dynamic groups of the role.
.SS Host and Device Assignment
.TP
.B add_host \fIrole\fR \fIhost\fR
Add a host to the role.
.TP
.B remove_host \fIrole\fR \fIhost\fR
Remove a host from the role.
.TP
.B list_hosts \fIrole\fR
List hosts assigned to the role.
.TP
.B add_device \fIrole\fR \fIdevice\fR
Add a device to the role.
.TP
.B remove_device \fIrole\fR \fIdevice\fR
Remove a device from the role.
.TP
.B list_devices \fIrole\fR
List devices assigned to the role.
.SS Dynamic Groups
.TP
.B add_dynamic_group \fIrole\fR \fIgroup\fR
Add a dynamic group to the role.
.TP
.B remove_dynamic_group \fIrole\fR \fIgroup\fR
Remove a dynamic group from the role.
.SS Sync Users
.TP
.B add_sync_user \fIrole\fR \fIuser\fR
Add a sync user to the role.
.TP
.B remove_sync_user \fIrole\fR \fIuser\fR
Remove a sync user from the role.
.TP
.B list_sync_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIrole\fR
List sync users of the role. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the role.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIrole\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the role.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBrole\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIrole\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the role.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIrole\fR
List the policies attached to the role.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
An ACL says what somebody may do with this role.
The somebody is a role or a token, never a user.
.PP
What the three forms \fIacl\fR, \fB+\fIacl\fR and \fB++\fIacl\fR mean, and which ACLs exist, is under \fBACLs\fR in
.BR otpme (7).
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.PP
The other direction, the ACLs this role holds on other objects, is \fBfind_acls\fR under \fBListing\fR above.
.TP
.B add_acl \fIrole\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR[\fB:\fIvalue\fR]
Give a role or a token an ACL on this role.
.br
\fIowner_type\fR is \fBrole\fR or \fBtoken\fR, and \fIowner\fR the path of that role or token.
An ACL may carry a value, for example \fBview:tokens\fR.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBadd:acl\fR.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIrole\fR \fIacl\fR
Take that ACL away again.
.br
Here the \fIacl\fR is the whole entry, owner and all, the way \fBlist_acls\fR prints it: \fBrole:berlin/sw\-admins:view\fR.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBdelete:acl\fR.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIrole\fR
Show the ACLs that lie on this role, i.e. who may do what with it.
Needs the ACL \fBview:acl\fR.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIrole\fR
Let the role inherit the default ACLs of the unit above it. It does not by default.
.RS
.PP
Only default ACLs are inherited. An ordinary ACL on the unit never is.
.PP
Moving a role into another unit is the one place that asks something else as well: the site admin role \fBSITE_ADMIN\fR gets neither the default ACLs of the new unit nor loses those of the old one.
.PP
Needs the ACL \fBenable:acl_inheritance\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIrole\fR
Stop inheriting them.
Only the ACLs on the role itself count from then on.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBdisable:acl_inheritance\fR.
.SS Extension and Attribute Management
.TP
.B add_extension \fIrole\fR \fIextension\fR
Add an extension to the role.
.TP
.B remove_extension \fIrole\fR \fIextension\fR
Remove an extension from the role.
.TP
.B add_attribute \fIrole\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Add an LDAP attribute to the role.
.TP
.B del_attribute \fIrole\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Remove an LDAP attribute from the role.
.TP
.B add_object_class \fIrole\fR \fIclass\fR
Add an LDAP object class to the role.
.TP
.B del_object_class \fIrole\fR \fIclass\fR
Remove an LDAP object class from the role.
.TP
.B show_ldif \fR[\fB\-a\fR \fIattributes\fR] \fIrole\fR
Show LDIF representation of the role. Use \fB\-a\fR to show only specific attributes.
.SS Configuration and Attributes
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIrole\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to default) or \fB\-a\fR to append the value to a list-typed parameter.
.TP
.B show_config \fIrole\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIrole\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIrole\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set role description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIrole\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.br
Without
.B \-\-language
the text is the administrator's own note about the object, which no user is ever shown. A text written with a language is one for the users of that language: a role named in
.B device_token_roles
shows it on the SSO portal, in the language of whoever is looking, see \fBotpme\fR(7).
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIrole\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIrole\fR
Show the changelog of the role.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIrole\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIrole\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIrole\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIrole\fR
Export role configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIrole\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all roles (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-token\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of tokens shown.
.TP
.B \-\-role\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of roles shown.
.TP
.B \-\-accessgroup\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of access groups shown.
.TP
.B \-\-group\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of groups shown.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Display specific attribute in list command.
.SS Token Options
.TP
.B \-i \fIinterfaces\fR
Limit login to given interfaces (e.g. tty, gui, ssh).
.TP
.B \-\-sign
Sign the object with default tags.
.TP
.B \-\-tags \fItag1,tag2\fR
Add tags to signature.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auto\-sign
Do not automatically sign when adding a token.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-sign
Do not remove any signature when removing a token.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving role.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.TP
.B \-r
List roles recursively.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH CONFIG PARAMETERS
Configuration parameters can be set with the \fBconfig\fR command and displayed with \fBshow_config\fR.
For a complete description of all available parameters and their applicable object types, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Managing Roles
.TP
.B otpme-role add admins
Create a new role
.TP
.B otpme-role add \-\-groups sysadmins \-\-roles operators
Create a role and add it to groups and roles
.SS Token Assignment
.TP
.B otpme-role add_token admins admin/totp
Add admin's TOTP token to the role
.TP
.B otpme-role add_token \-i ssh admins admin/ssh_key
Add SSH key for SSH interface only
.SS Role Nesting
.TP
.B otpme-role add_role super_admins admins
Add admins role as child of super_admins
.TP
.B otpme-role list_roles \-r super_admins
List all nested roles recursively
.SS VLAN Assignment
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add_role employees_vlan employees
Put every member of the role into a VLAN
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add_role admin_vlan admins
Give a role nested in "employees" a VLAN of its own. Its members get it
instead of the VLAN of "employees"
.SS Policy Assignment
.TP
.B otpme-role add_policy admins require_2fa
Attach a policy to the role
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
